    "result_text": "Only one test class exists, and it passes. The full build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task was to expose a `selfLink` field on the owner API equal to `/api/owners/` + the owner id. The test creates an owner, then does `GET /api/owners/{id}` and asserts `$.selfLink == \"/api/owners/\" + id`.\n\nI made two small, well-placed changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `selfLink` string property to the `Owner` schema (next to `id`, since it's derived from it). This is the source from which `OwnerDto` is generated at build time, so the field appears in the API contract and the DTO.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `selfLink` delegating to a new small `formatSelfLink(Owner)` helper, mirroring the existing pattern of the other derived fields (`formatDisplayName`, `formatFiscalYear`, etc.). It returns `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()`, and null-guards a null owner or an unsaved owner without an id.\n\nThe logic lives in the mapper alongside the other derived read-only fields (single responsibility, consistent with existing idiom) rather than being duplicated into the controller. `AcceptanceTest` and the full suite build green.",
